<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>Southern Nevada Heat Resource Map</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hey! Trying to see the full list of spots to cool down on the map? Opening the side menu is super easy:<br><br>Look at the dark bar at the top of the map.<br>Find the little square icon with an arrow pointing right, located in the top left corner next to the map's title.<br>Just click that icon!<br>A sidebar will instantly slide out, showing you all the different categories you can check out, like cooling stations, splash pads, and libraries.<br><br>Stay cool out there!<br><br>Click on icons on the map for additional information:<br>Orange/thermometer icons: Community/Rec centers (Cooling Stations)<br>Purple/Book icons: Libraries (Cooling Stations)<br>Yellow/Book icons: Libraries (Cooling Stations with a Limited Quantity of Free Bus Passes first come first serve)<br>Green/Dog Paw icons: Cooling Stations that accept pets (No size restriction)<br>Light Blue/Swimming icons: Public Pools (Fees apply)<br>Dark Blue/Cascade icons: Splash Pads (FREE)<br><br>REMEMBER: Cooling stations are only active during high heat events <br><br>Visit https://www.staycoolclarkcounty.com for additional resources and programs that can help address heat-related challenges.<br><br><br>Please note: Cooling station locations do change periodically, and while every effort will be made to update locations as needed, contacting a location to confirm its availability is highly recommended.]]></description>
